247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Conventional ARINC 429 communication controllers are designed to transmit and receive data with basic error detection, such as parity checking. However, they cannot continuously monitor the health of the communication channel or distinguish between temporary and repeated communication faults. This can reduce the reliability of aircraft communication systems. Therefore, there is a need for a hardware-based communication controller that can detect faults, monitor communication health, and automatically perform suitable recovery actions to improve reliability and system performance.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
